  "published": "2026-10-08T00:25:34.26Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.4.0: Render(\"PPTX\") writes editable PowerPoint slides: text boxes, PowerPoint tables, shapes and connectors glued to their boxes, pictures, slide numbers, speaker notes, layouts and placeholders. ReportImport (.NET 8 and later) turns Markdown and Marp decks, with Mermaid flowcharts, and the reports of FastReport, Telerik, ActiveReports, DevExpress, Stimulsoft, Crystal Reports, Microsoft Access, JasperReports, BIRT, QuickReport, ReportBuilder, Visual Basic 6, PowerBuilder and Visual FoxPro into RDLC. SSRS2's own report extensions, which Report Viewer skips: barcodes (QR, Swiss QR-bill, EPC, Data Matrix, PDF417, Aztec, Code 128, GS1-128, EAN, UPC and more), rounded corners, ellipses, diamonds and cylinders, arrowheads, a table's header rows on every page. Word: the FlowLayout setting writes a document Word edits as its own (paragraphs, heading styles, tables, drawings, header, footer, footnotes). LocalReport.CheckRendering() and ReportOutput (.NET 8 and later) say what a report does not render as written and read a written deck or document back. Emoji, no-break spaces, Chinese, Japanese and Korean fonts and right-to-left text drawn as Report Viewer draws them. Details: https://ssrs2.net",
